  "comment": "Class-level parentlessRole (SCHEMA.md \"Node structure\", owner 2026-10-24): class.create/class.update carry the OPTIONAL NULLABLE parentlessRole \u2014 \"block\" = a parentless member of the class renders in the Block role (block chrome, no document chrome) instead of with document chrome; absent/null = \"page\", the zero-migration default. Presence writes, present-null clears, exactly like color. The flag is a RENDER CONTRACT read only in the cascade's parentless branch (the is_embedded symmetry: the embedding flag is read only for parented nodes) \u2014 the applier maps it without validating (PC1), and it is EXTENDS-AWARE at read time: a class effectively carries \"block\" when its own flag OR any extends-ancestor's is \"block\" (one-way demote; no per-level unflag). This fixture pins the payload shapes: Task seeds flagged block; Event is flagged by a class.update, then CLEARED by a present-null update (back to the page default); Errand carries no flag of its own but extends the flagged Task \u2014 its effective role derives from the chain, not from a stored value. The standalone task object.create is the population the role bends: a parentless node created with classIds [Task] reads Block-role on every client.",
